{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And you shall clothe them — Aaron.</b> Those mentioned for Aaron — choshen, and ephod, and robe, and tunic of chequered work, turban, and sash, and tzitz, and breeches — that are written below among them all." "<b>And his sons with him.</b> Those written in connection with them." "<b>And you shall anoint them.</b> Aaron and his sons with the anointing oil." "<b>And you shall fill their hand.</b> Every מִלּוּי יָדַיִם is an expression of inauguration — when one enters a matter to be established in it from that day onward. And in la'az: when one appoints a man over the oversight of a matter, the ruler places in his hand a leather glove, which they call גאנ\"ט בְּלַעַ\"ז, and by his hand he holds him in the matter; and they call that handing-over רווישט\"יר בְּלַעַ\"ז — and that is מִלּוּי יָדַיִם."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {3 "גאנ\"ט is Old French gant ('glove'); רווישט\"יר is Old French investir ('investiture')."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:26.134485301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}